ORIGIN AND ATTRIBUTION

This skill was developed for Seth J. Chandler as an expanded derivative of his local
"volokh-claim-assessor" skill. It uses the novelty, nonobviousness, utility, soundness,
and test-suite concepts attributed in SKILL.md to Eugene Volokh's published academic-
writing work. The Apache-2.0 license covers the original skill instructions and bundled
resources in this package; it does not license or reproduce Volokh's book or article.

The derivative adds role-specific assessment modes; claim crystallization; capability-
aware and connector-aware research routing; public-source and no-connector fallbacks;
preemption mapping; claim-type-specific tests; a sustainable double-pass scholarly red
team; complete-report delivery requirements; and differentiated revision paths for
professors, student notes, and seminar papers.

The double-pass adversarial discipline was also influenced by the independently named
"sustainable-opposing-counsel-review" workflow. That companion skill is optional and is
not bundled or required; this package contains a self-contained version of the method.

No affiliation with or endorsement by Eugene Volokh, Lawve, any research provider, or
the authors or operators of cited tools and services is claimed.

BUNDLED CODE

This package contains no executable code. It makes no network calls itself and handles no
credentials. Research access, if any, is supplied and controlled by the user's host.

